      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A pure free speech advocate would argue that \"protection\" in this context is a convenient euphemism for viewpoint discrimination, which is the very definition of censorship. They contend that the best defense against misinformation or hate is more robust debate and education, a process that requires the unhindered flow of all speech, good and bad. By defining \"misinformation,\" the state inherently gains the power to declare certain opinions illegitimate, which is a dangerous form of ideological control.",
